{
 "_comment": "FLUX 2 WITH THREE REFERENCES AND AN EXPLICIT CANVAS - the local @CHARAC1 + @CHARAC2 + @PLACE compositor. Built from 68_flux2_ref by adding a third ReferenceLatent stage and replacing the GetImageSize canvas with width/height numbers. Each reference is scaled to 1 MP, VAE-encoded and chained into the conditioning, so the pictures carry identity, wardrobe and place while the prompt carries only what is happening. This is the breakdown's REFS -> START FRAME step (Alter Anime Studio, Vol. 01), done with local weights; the start frame it makes is what LTX-2.5 or H3 animates.",
 "_notes": [
  "42 = reference one, 46 = reference two, ref3 = reference three. Order is the chain order; the canvas no longer depends on any of them.",
  "sg1_48 and sg1_47 carry the canvas (width, height). 1280x720 by default - 0.9 MP, which is the LTX_SAFE rung that allows a 30 s shot.",
  "sg1_6 is the prompt. Name the references by role (\"the striker\", \"the guard\", \"the court\"), never by appearance: a description competes with the picture (measured, playbook §95 S1).",
  "sg1_25 is the seed; 9 the output prefix; sg1_95 true = 8-step turbo LoRA, false = 20 steps.",
  "No negative prompt: Flux 2 runs through BasicGuider. Say everything positively.",
  "Driven by studio/_tools/fight.py --anchors."
 ],
